From b6fe2b769d9b7f69ad38587ec4e494e388eb9156 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 23:55:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix mobile-responsiveness bugs across shell nav, tables, and
 calendars

Critical: clamp FloatingPanel width to viewport (worker config panels
overflowed off-screen on phones), add workspace switching and sign-out
to the mobile nav menu (previously desktop-only via PrimaryRail), give
the Teammates page a single-pane mobile layout with a back button
instead of a fixed-width rail squeezing the chat, and make the home
workspace table scroll horizontally instead of clipping columns.

High: wrap tables that were missing overflow-x-auto (client rosters,
leak-map/pre-call-read run views, module-view lists), scroll the
hardcoded 7-column month calendars horizontally instead of crushing
cell content, stack the Settings > Apps sidebar and SMTP form fields
on mobile, and let queue-row action buttons wrap instead of overflowing.

Medium: make hover-only controls (tag delete, roster row menu) visible
below md since touch has no hover state, and enlarge several sub-40px
tap targets (toggle switch, icon dropdown trigger, tour launcher,
workspace card menu). Also fixes Sheet's hardcoded dark-mode-only text
colors, which made client-details-drawer's title invisible in light mode.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Lv1Fc4mc6LHrFpMHiHajTt
